  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This dish uses boiled chickpea flour dumplings called "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "gatte",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "gatte"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " set in a sharp "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "yoghurt gravy",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "yoghurt-gravy"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " finished with a hot spice oil called "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "tadka ",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "tadka"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". The yoghurt must be whisked smooth before adding to the pan or it will split."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Add the gatte to the gravy just before serving. Long simmering makes them absorb liquid and turn very soft. A short simmer keeps them firm with a little chew."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
